WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.756
Idea. No real number squared is negative. Three squared is nine, and minus three, all squared, is also nine. So no real number squares to minus nineteen. A root is a value of x that makes an expression zero. A real root is a root that is a real number.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:32.181
The discriminant tells you how many real roots a quadratic has. For a x squared plus b x plus c, it is b squared minus four a c. Positive means two roots, zero means one, negative means none.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:43.968
Now a cubic. If it is x minus k times a quadratic, and the quadratic has no real roots, the only real root is k. The curve crosses the x axis once.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:01:00.369
The question says hence show that there is only one real root. Hence means use the result from the part before. Show that means the result is given, and your working must prove it. Divide, find the discriminant, say what it means, and name the root.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:10.695
Method. Step one: divide by the known factor to get the quadratic. Step two: work out b squared minus four a c, showing the numbers.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:19.733
Step three: state that it is negative, so no real roots. Step four: the only real root comes from the linear factor. Name it.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.139
The trap is writing the negative number and stopping. Always write what it means.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:39.600
Worked example. June twenty twenty two. From part a, p is four and q is ten, and x plus one is a factor. Hence show that f of x equals zero has only one real root. Three marks.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:51.791
Step one: the quadratic. Write x plus one, times x squared plus b x plus c. The constants give c equals seven. The x squared terms give b equals three.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:02:00.199
Step two: the discriminant. Here a is one, b is three, c is seven. Nine minus twenty eight is minus nineteen.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:07.539
Step three: say what it means. Minus nineteen is less than zero, so the quadratic has no real roots.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:17.654
A tempting wrong route is b squared plus four a c. That gives thirty seven, which wrongly suggests two real roots. The discriminant has a minus.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:33.726
So the only real root is x equals minus one. Check: f of minus one is minus one, plus four, minus ten, plus seven, which is zero. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:46.870
Common mistake. A common mistake is to write minus nineteen and stop. You must say it is less than zero, so no real roots, so the only real root is x equals minus one.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:03:01.343
Your turn. Now you try, from June twenty twenty four. Part a showed that a equals twenty one. Now show that the curve meets the x axis only once. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:14.091
Answer. Write f of x as three x minus two, times two x squared plus b x plus five. The x squared terms give b equals minus three. The x terms check.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:24.655
The discriminant: a is two, b is minus three, c is five. Nine minus forty is minus thirty one. That is less than zero, so no real roots.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:36.758
So the only real root is x equals two thirds. The curve meets the x axis once. A common wrong answer writes minus three squared as minus nine, losing the bracket.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.629
Remember: quadratic, discriminant, meaning, and the one real root.
